# ==============================================================================
# TIO IntentOperand Extension
# ==============================================================================
#
# Purpose:
#   This file extends TM Forum Intent Ontology (TIO) v3.6.0 with semantic
#   classification for valid Intent boolean function operands.
#
# Rationale:
#   TIO 3.6.0 enforces a hierarchy: Intent -> Expectation -> Condition
#   Intents can only directly reference Expectations in their boolean functions.
#   Conditions must be wrapped in PropertyExpectation.
#
#   Currently this is validated by checking "NOT a Condition" using:
#   ?argList rdf:rest*/rdf:first ?condition .
#   ?condition a log:Condition .
#
#   This extension provides positive validation ("IS an IntentOperand") which:
#   - Is more extensible as new Expectation types are added
#   - Provides clearer semantic documentation of valid hierarchy
#   - Enables consistent validation patterns across the ontology
#
# Design:
#   These extensions are separated from the TIO baseline to:
#   - Keep TIO 3.6.0 ontology files pristine and unchanged
#   - Enable clean merging of future TIO updates
#   - Simplify proposing these additions upstream to TM Forum
#
# Compatibility:
#   - Backward compatible: All existing valid intents remain valid
#   - Forward compatible: New Expectation subclasses automatically inherit
#   - Zero breaking changes to TIO 3.6.0 semantics
#
# ==============================================================================

@prefix icm:  <http://tio.models.tmforum.org/tio/v3.6.0/IntentCommonModel/> .
@prefix log:  <http://tio.models.tmforum.org/tio/v3.6.0/LogicalOperators/> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# ==============================================================================
# SECTION 1: Core Class Definition
# ==============================================================================
#
# The icm:IntentOperand mixin class identifies entities that can be directly
# referenced as operands in Intent boolean functions (log:allOf, log:anyOf, etc).
#
# Intent hierarchy: Intent -> Expectation -> Condition
# - Intents can ONLY reference Expectations (IntentOperand)
# - Expectations can reference both Expectations AND Conditions (ExpectationOperand)
# - Conditions must be wrapped in PropertyExpectation to be used in Intents
#
# ==============================================================================

icm:IntentOperand
  rdfs:label "Intent Operand Class"@en ;
  rdfs:comment """Things that can be directly referenced as operands in Intent boolean functions.

  Intents can only directly reference Expectations (not Conditions).
  Conditions must be wrapped in PropertyExpectation.

  Intent hierarchy: Intent -> Expectation -> Condition
  - Intent log:allOf/anyOf can reference Expectations (IntentOperand)
  - PropertyExpectation log:allOf/anyOf can reference Conditions

  SHACL validation uses positive checking (IS IntentOperand) instead of
  negative checking (NOT Condition) for clearer semantics and extensibility."""@en ;
  rdf:type rdfs:Class
.

icm:ExpectationOperand
  rdfs:label "Expectation Operand Class"@en ;
  rdfs:comment """Things that can be referenced as operands in Expectation boolean functions.

  PropertyExpectations can reference both Conditions and other Expectations.
  This is a broader class than IntentOperand."""@en ;
  rdf:type rdfs:Class
.

# ==============================================================================
# SECTION 2: Intent Common Model Extensions
# ==============================================================================
#
# Mark Expectation as IntentOperand (valid for Intent boolean functions).
# Mark Condition as ExpectationOperand but NOT IntentOperand (enforces hierarchy).
#
# ==============================================================================

# Expectations are valid operands for both Intent and Expectation boolean functions
icm:Expectation
  rdfs:subClassOf icm:IntentOperand ;
  rdfs:subClassOf icm:ExpectationOperand .

# Conditions are valid operands ONLY for Expectation boolean functions
# NOTE: log:Condition is intentionally NOT marked as IntentOperand
# This enforces the hierarchy: Conditions must be wrapped in PropertyExpectation
log:Condition
  rdfs:subClassOf icm:ExpectationOperand .

# ==============================================================================
# SECTION 3: Vocabulary Extension
# ==============================================================================
#
# Adds extension terms to icm:Vocabulary so they are recognized by vocabulary
# validation constraints.
#
# ==============================================================================

icm:Vocabulary
  rdfs:member icm:IntentOperand ,
              icm:ExpectationOperand .

# ==============================================================================
# End of IntentOperandExtension.ttl
# ==============================================================================
